From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Collectives: env cap on one-shot collective eligibility

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm@6d66eed35b0ab1cc0e05f00e83ef638ba10ae3db
with the 1126 release series (0709 included). The single choke points in
vllm/distributed/device_communicators/cuda_communicator.py are the all_gather,
reduce_scatter and all_to_all_rows delegations to the one-shot adapter.

Rationale: sparknet 0.6.0's multi-stage kernels accept arbitrarily large
payloads whose per-row pack fits a slot (oneshot/runtime.py
should_reduce_scatter: ``world_size * row_bytes <= _slot_bytes`` outside CUDA
graph capture), so large sequence-parallel prefill collectives leave the
PyNCCL path — the path the 2026-11-21 2 MiB NCCL_BUFFSIZE alignment
accelerated by +1.7-2.3% at 131K. The measured cost was a repeatable -3.0%
prefill at 131K (experiments/2026-11-26-sparknet-060).
SPARK_DS41F_ONESHOT_MAX_BYTES restores the 0.5.0 single-slot boundary at the
dispatch level: unset or 0 leaves sparknet 0.6.0's eligibility unchanged, a
byte value caps one-shot eligibility so larger payloads fall back to PyNCCL
as 0.5.0 did.

Quality: dispatch-only; a capped collective takes the same PyNCCL path 0.5.0
took, with identical arithmetic (the rank-order reduce-scatter keeps
bit-identical sums; cuda_communicator already routes there). No kernel,
buffer or numerics change.

Tests: release tests; the 2026-11-26-sparknet-060-cap window measures the
capped arm's prefill recovery (gate: 131K back at the production level) and
decode parity, plus the temperature-0 determinism gate.

Upstream status: local deployment policy; not submitted (depends on our
NCCL_BUFFSIZE tuning and the 0.6.0 eligibility change).
---
 vllm/distributed/device_communicators/cuda_communicator.py | 22 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/cuda_communicator.py b/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/cuda_communicator.py
--- a/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/cuda_communicator.py
+++ b/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/cuda_communicator.py
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
 
 
+import os
 from typing import TYPE_CHECKING
 
 import torch
@@ -79,6 +80,21 @@
         comm.destroy()
 
 
+
+_ONESHOT_MAX_BYTES = int(os.environ.get("SPARK_DS41F_ONESHOT_MAX_BYTES", "0") or "0")
+
+
+def _oneshot_within_cap(t: torch.Tensor) -> bool:
+    """Env cap on one-shot collective eligibility (unset or 0: uncapped).
+
+    sparknet 0.6.0's multi-stage kernels accept arbitrarily large payloads
+    whose per-row pack fits a slot, displacing the PyNCCL path the 2 MiB
+    NCCL_BUFFSIZE alignment accelerates; the cap restores the 0.5.0
+    single-slot boundary at the dispatch level.
+    """
+    return _ONESHOT_MAX_BYTES <= 0 or t.numel() * t.element_size() <= _ONESHOT_MAX_BYTES
+
+
 class CudaCommunicator(DeviceCommunicatorBase):
     b12x_ar_comm: "B12xPcieAllReduce | SparknetOneShotAllReduce | None"
 
@@ -649,6 +665,7 @@
             and not b12x_ar_comm.disabled
             and should_all_gather is not None
             and should_all_gather(input_, dim)
+            and _oneshot_within_cap(input_)
         ):
             assert all_gather is not None
             return all_gather(input_, dim)
@@ -705,6 +722,7 @@
             and not b12x_ar_comm.disabled
             and should_a2a is not None
             and should_a2a(input_, rows)
+            and _oneshot_within_cap(input_)
         ):
             assert a2a is not None
             return a2a(input_, rows)
@@ -733,6 +751,7 @@
             and not b12x_ar_comm.disabled
             and should_rs is not None
             and should_rs(input_, dim)
+            and _oneshot_within_cap(input_)
         ):
             assert rs is not None
             return rs(input_, dim)
